{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/String/Lossy.html#String.fromUTF8Lossy\"><span class=\"name\">String</span>.<span class=\"name\">fromUTF8Lossy</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#ByteArray\">ByteArray</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Decodes a sequence of characters from their UTF-8 representation, replacing invalid byte\nsequences with `�` (`U+FFFD`, the Unicode replacement character). Whenever decoding fails at some\nbyte, that byte and all immediately following continuation bytes are replaced by a single `�`.\n\nExamples:\n * `String.fromUTF8Lossy [0x4C, 0xE2, 0x88, 0x83, 0x4E].toByteArray = \"L∃N\"`\n * `String.fromUTF8Lossy [0x61, 0xFF, 0x62].toByteArray = \"a�b\"`, since `0xFF` never occurs in\n   UTF-8.\n * `String.fromUTF8Lossy [0x61, 0xE2, 0x88, 0x62].toByteArray = \"a�b\"`, since the three-byte\n   sequence starting with `0xE2` is truncated.\n * `String.fromUTF8Lossy [0x61, 0xED, 0xA0, 0x80, 0x62].toByteArray = \"a�b\"`, since\n   `0xED 0xA0 0x80` would encode the surrogate code point `U+D800`, which is not a valid `Char`.\n * `String.fromUTF8Lossy [0x61, 0x80, 0x80, 0x80, 0x62].toByteArray = \"a�b\"`, since a run of\n   stray continuation bytes is replaced by a single `�`.\n * `String.fromUTF8Lossy [0xFF, 0xFF].toByteArray = \"��\"`","docLink":"./Init/Data/String/Lossy.html#String.fromUTF8Lossy","kind":"def","line":27,"name":"String.fromUTF8Lossy","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Init/Data/String/Lossy.lean#L27-L57"}}],"imports":["Init.Data.String.Basic","Init.Data.String.Decode","Init.Omega","Init.WFTactics"],"instances":[],"name":"Init.Data.String.Lossy"}